WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.990
A virus is tiny.

2
00:00:02.040 --> 00:00:06.740
Most viruses are 10 to 100
times smaller than a bacterium.

3
00:00:06.790 --> 00:00:08.430
It has no metabolism.

4
00:00:08.480 --> 00:00:09.670
It cannot feed.

5
00:00:09.720 --> 00:00:11.040
It cannot grow.

6
00:00:11.090 --> 00:00:12.760
And it never divides.

7
00:00:12.810 --> 00:00:16.740
Yet catch influenza, and
symptoms can appear within days.

8
00:00:16.790 --> 00:00:20.320
So if a virus cannot feed, grow or divide,

9
00:00:20.370 --> 00:00:23.150
how does one virus become millions?

10
00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:25.940
In this mission, you'll
take a virus apart:

11
00:00:25.990 --> 00:00:28.950
its genes, and the
protein coat around them.

12
00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:31.690
Then you'll meet a virus
that attacks bacteria,

13
00:00:31.740 --> 00:00:34.370
with a tail that injects its DNA.

14
00:00:34.420 --> 00:00:39.890
Your mission: find out how one virus,
which cannot divide, becomes millions.
